# Weekend Yahoo Finance Fallback Plan

We will update the `fetchAssetIntervalData` to handle BingX weekend pauses by falling back directly to Yahoo Finance's `.chart` API.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] `index.js`
We will rewrite `fetchAssetIntervalData`:
1. It will first attempt to fetch prices from BingX.
2. If BingX returns an empty list (which triggers our `Market for ... is currently paused` error), the `catch` block will automatically trigger the Yahoo Finance `.chart()` fallback strategy.
3. The Yahoo Finance fallback will utilize `yahooFinance.chart(fetchId, { interval, period1 })` to securely fetch the latest available `15m`, `60m` (for `1h` and `4h`) data without encountering the standard `historical` API enum errors.

## User Review Required
Does this fallback hierarchy make sense? Once approved, I will deploy the fail-safe directly to the AWS server.
